// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/person_naming.t27 -- how a person is named on a screen, and what stands there
; when the name is not known
; One boundary, and it is the last one before a customer reads about somebody: given what the
; shop recorded about a person, WHAT STRING goes in the slot reserved for their name. This file
; owns the parts a name may be built from, the three outcomes that boundary has, the rule that a
; fallback must be recognisable AS a fallback, and the rule that an identifier is not a name. It
; owns no wording in any language, no locale, no identity proof, no gate, no price and no screen
; layout: four sibling contracts own those and are named by ID below, not one of them restated.
; Nor does it own the attendee normaliser's handle-length bound: turbobaby/events-booking owns
; that, and a fifth edge below names it. (Corrected 2026-09-22: until then this header counted
; four edges while the file held that fifth owner's ID in a constant outside its edge block and
; restated its bound in four constants and three functions of its own -- restating an owner,
; which the sentence above says this file does to none of the four it names.)
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). src/trios/person.rs is 345 lines that no contract named, and the
; subject it decides had already produced the defect its own header describes: the friends panel
; printed the English noun and a four-digit tail for every invitee, because user_languages
; .first_name was empty for essentially everybody, because the only function that wrote it had no
; callers at all. That is a D9 shape -- an absent value answered with a confident constant -- and
; the constant was a person's name, so what the shop asserted was not a rounding error but a
; false record: it told a customer that these people were on file when they were not.
; --
; THE HEADER WAS VERIFIED RATHER THAN QUOTED, and it is out of date in the direction that matters.
; save_user_name has ZERO definitions in the tree today: grep -rn "fn save_user_name" over src/,
; tests/ and migrations/ returns nothing, and over that same scope the SIX surviving mentions are
; all prose describing what was removed -- src/bot/mod.rs:95, src/db/mod.rs:951, src/db/users.rs:5,
; src/trios/person.rs:5, tests/integration_invitee_names.rs:5 and migrations/073_user_identity
; .sql:5. The count read FIVE until the review of 2026-09-21: the migration comment was missed by
; a sweep whose stated scope already included migrations/, which is the cheapest way a census goes
; wrong -- a grep narrower than the sentence describing it.
; The writer that replaced it, save_user_identity at src/db/mod.rs:963, has ONE production caller
; -- remember_who at src/bot/mod.rs:111 -- and that caller is invoked from THREE places, one per
; kind of update Telegram delivers: src/bot/callbacks.rs:134, src/bot/commands.rs:169 and
; src/bot/handlers.rs:30. migrations/073_user_identity.sql added last_name and username and
; backfilled both from orders. So the defect the header narrates in the present tense is closed,
; and the header still reads as though it were open. The measurement is recorded below in both
; halves, because a reader who trusted the prose would contract a bug that no longer exists and a
; reader who trusted only the prose's absence would miss that the rule it argues for is real.
; --
; WHERE THE RULE LIVES, AND WHY IT IS AN ARGUMENT THIS CORPUS KEEPS MAKING. src/lib.rs:108 puts
; pub mod db behind cfg(all(not(target_arch = "wasm32"), feature = "backend")) and src/lib.rs:17-18
; puts pub mod ui behind cfg(target_arch = "wasm32"); Cargo.toml:174 sets default = [], so a bare
; cargo test compiles NEITHER. src/lib.rs:13 declares pub mod trios unconditionally. A naming rule
; written in the query or in the component is therefore a rule cargo test cannot execute, and the
; one end-to-end witness there is, tests/integration_invitee_names.rs, is gated twice over -- a
; crate-level cfg(feature = "backend") at :20 and #[ignore] at :103 -- so it does not run either
; unless somebody asks for it by name with a database attached. Several contracts in this corpus
; exist for exactly this reason, and this one states the reason rather than inheriting it.
; --
; THE SECOND MEASUREMENT, and it is why this file counts sites instead of trusting the owner.
; FOURTEEN functions in src/ decide what stands in the name slot when the name is absent. ONE of
; them goes through the module that owns the rule. TEN answer with a bare English noun carrying no
; distinguishing tail -- which is the original defect, alive at ten further addresses, in SQL
; COALESCE arms, in unwrap_or_else on an absent column and in unwrap_or_else on a FAILED QUERY,
; where the stand-in additionally hides an error behind a plausible person. One builds its label
; out of the identifier, so it is at least distinguishable. One returns nothing at all and lets the
; screen ask the customer, which is the only shape here that invents nothing. One prints a number
; under a label that says it is an identifier, which is admissible and is the distinction this
; whole file turns on. The first count attempted for this paragraph was SEVEN, reached by reading
; the obvious surfaces; the sweep that produced fourteen is written into CENSUS_METHOD below, and
; the wrong seven is recorded in CENSUS_FIRST_ATTEMPT because a census whose method is not stated
; is a number that cannot be re-derived or refuted.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES, and in this file the refusal is the subject. It carries NO PERSON:
; not a name, not a surname, not a handle, not a telegram id, not a fragment of one, and not in a
; test fixture either -- a contract about naming people that shipped with a person's name in it
; would be precisely the leak it exists to prevent, and D14 (DECISIONS.md:186-200) lists renter
; names and telegram handles first among the fields this repository must never contain in any
; form. Every fixture below is an abstract count, a bucket index or a boolean. It quotes no user
; copy in any language: the screens it describes are full of Cyrillic and every string is cited by
; its i18n KEY NAME, never by its text (L3), so nothing here can be used to reinstate a wording.
; It holds no fallback word, because holding one would make this file a translation table. It
; decides no locale, no fallback locale and no key total (turbobaby/locale-policy), proves no
; identity and names no gate (turbobaby/request-identity), states no numeric absence discipline of
; its own (turbobaby/pricing-honesty, whose shape this follows for a string instead of a number)
; and rules on no screen's claims (turbobaby/customer-surface). It publishes no count of how many
; rows are nameless today, and says so in a named refusal rather than estimating one.
; RE-POINTED 2026-09-24: every src/db/mod.rs line this file cites past line 385 moved four lines
; down when migrations/087_delivery_zones_phuket.sql joined MIGRATIONS, and four more with
; migrations/088_unpublish_events.sql the same day; re-measured, and nothing they point at changed.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-person-naming;

